{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 66, :comments ["<b>Achiezer son of Amishaddai.</b> Perhaps he alluded to Samson, and his saying <b>achi</b> ('my brother') alludes to the spirit of YHWH that was upon him, as it is written (Judges 14:6) ״וַתִּצְלַח עָלָיו רוּחַ ה׳״, and it corresponds to the name achi in the manner of the verse's saying (Psalms 122:8) ״לְמַעַן אַחַי וְרֵעָי״. <b>Ezer</b> ('help') — because YHWH was his help against his enemies. And his saying <b>son of Amishaddai</b> alludes to after the Philistines gouged out his eyes and he called to YHWH and He was with him and he took vengeance upon his enemies."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:43.580094555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}